<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camera degli Sposi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1465–<a href="/years/1474">1474</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Camera degli Sposi ('Bridal Chamber') is a room in the Castle of San Giorgio in Mantua frescoed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-mantegna">Andrea Mantegna</a> between about 1465 and 1474 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-iii-gonzaga">Ludovico III Gonzaga</a>. Its walls show the marquis with his family and court, and its ceiling has a painted oculus opening on to the sky, one of the first such illusionistic views from below in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> painting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/camera-degli-sposi.jpg" alt="Camera degli Sposi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gonzaloferjar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mantegna_-_Camera_degli_Sposi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
